# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build a bit-flip stabilizer circuit {#build-a-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuit}"
msgstr "Bina litar penstabil bit-flip {#build-a-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bit-flip code is among the simplest examples of a stabilizer code. It "
"protects the state against a single bit-flip (X) error on any of the "
"encoding qubits. Consider the action of bit-flip error $X$, which maps "
"$|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow "
"|0\\rangle$ on any of our qubits, then we have $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, E_1, E_2"
" \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. The code requires five qubits: three are used "
"to encode the protected state, and the remaining two are used as stabilizer "
"measurement ancillas.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod bit-flip adalah antara contoh kod penstabil yang paling mudah. Ia "
"melindungi keadaan daripada ralat bit-flip (X) tunggal pada mana-mana qubit "
"pengekodan. Pertimbangkan tindakan ralat bit-flip $X$, yang memetakan "
"$|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow "
"|0\\rangle$ pada mana-mana qubit kita, maka kita ada $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, "
"E_1, E_2 \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. Kod ini memerlukan lima qubit: tiga "
"digunakan untuk mengekodkan keadaan yang dilindungi, dan dua yang lain "
"digunakan sebagai ancilla pengukuran penstabil.\n"

